# Data Provider Patterns

## Core Pattern

**ALWAYS use the IDataProvider interface** - this is the foundation for all data access in the codebase.

## Provider Types

### 1. AppSync Provider (Production)

```typescript
// Use for AWS AppSync GraphQL queries
export const useEnrollmentsProvider = (): IDataProvider<ProviderData> => {
  return useAmplifyAppsyncProvider('GetEnrollmentsByAgentByMonthEnrolledView')
}
```

### 2. Local Dev Provider (Development)

```typescript
// Use for local development with static/mock data
export const useEnrollmentStaticProvider = <T>(params: LocalDevProviderParams<T>): IDataProvider<T> => {
  const _postProcess = (data: T[], params?: any): T[] => {
    // Add filtering/transformation logic
    if (params?.start_date) {
      data = data.filter(item => /* filter logic */)
    }
    return data
  }
  return useLocalDevProvider({...params, postProcess: _postProcess})
}
```

### 3. Static Data Provider

```typescript
// For loading static JSON files
const provider = useStaticDataProvider<T>('~~/tests/mocks/data.json')
```

### 4. Storage Data Provider

```typescript
// For sessionStorage-based data
const provider = useStorageDataProvider<T>('storeKey', 'id')
```

## Post-Processing Pattern

When creating local dev providers, use post-processing for filtering:

```typescript
const _postProcess = (data: T[], params?: any): T[] => {
  if (Object.keys(params).includes('start_date')) {
    const start = toYM(params.start_date)
    data = data.filter(item => {
      const ym = toYM(item['date_enrolled'])
      return ym >= start
    })
  }
  if (Object.keys(params).includes('end_date')) {
    const end = toYM(params.end_date)
    data = data.filter(item => {
      const ym = toYM(item['date_enrolled'])
      return ym <= end
    })
  }
  logger.debug('Post processed data:', data)
  return data
}
```

## Provider Factory Pattern

Create provider factories that return the appropriate provider based on environment:

```typescript
export const useEnrollmentsProvider = (): IDataProvider<ProviderData> => {
  // Returns AppSync provider for production
  return useAmplifyAppsyncProvider('GetEnrollmentsByAgentByMonthEnrolledView')
}

export const useEnrollmentStaticProvider = <T>(params: LocalDevProviderParams<T>): IDataProvider<T> => {
  // Returns local dev provider with post-processing
  const _postProcess = (data: T[], params?: any): T[] => {
    // Post-processing logic
  }
  return useLocalDevProvider({...params, postProcess: _postProcess})
}
```

## Important Notes

- **Always implement IDataProvider interface** - fetch, create, update, delete, reset
- **Throw ManagedError** for unsupported operations
- **Use post-processing** for local dev providers to match production behavior
- **Check existing providers** before creating new ones
- **Use logger** for debugging provider operations
- **Return ProccessedData format** with `{ data, errors }` structure
